        "content": "<p>netliomax25-code opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14884\">PR #14884</a> from <code>netliomax25-code:wasi-nn-witx-guest-error-trap</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The WITX wasi-nn host panics when a guest passes a bad pointer or a non-UTF-8 string, because <code>nn_errno_from_wasi_nn_error</code> hits <code>unimplemented!()</code> for <code>WasiNnError::GuestError</code>. For example, <code>load_by_name</code> with a name pointer past the end of linear memory takes down the host with \"not implemented: guest error conversion\" instead of failing the call.</p>\n<p>This returns the <code>GuestError</code> as a trap. Invalid enum arguments already trap in the wiggle glue, and WASIp1 traps on out-of-bounds pointers, so this follows the same model. The new unit test calls <code>load_by_name</code> with an out-of-bounds pointer and with invalid UTF-8; it panics before this change and passes after.</p>\n<p>Tested with <code>cargo test -p wasmtime-wasi-nn --lib</code>, with and without default features.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633295537,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792498152
    },
